   # along diagonals of constant (column - row). Infer its period from\n    # the stroke spacing, then extend that sequence over the grid.\n    points = [(c-r, grid[r][c])\n              for r in range(h) for c in range(w) if grid[r][c]]\n\n    best = None\n    for p in range(2, min(h, w) + 1):\n        buckets = {}\n        for d, color in points:\n            buckets.setdefault(d % p, set()).add(color)\n        # Prefer the shortest period with a clear majority color per class.\n        score = sum(max((sum(1 for d, col in points\n                         if d % p == k and col == v)\n                        for v in buckets[k]), default=0)\n                    for k in buckets)\n        if best is None or score > best[0]:\n            best = (score, p, buckets)\n\n    _, p, buckets = best\n    seq = {}\n    for k, colors in buckets.items():\n        counts = {}\n        for d, color in points:\n            if d % p == k:\n                counts[color] = counts.get(color, 0) + 1\n        seq[k] = max(counts, key=counts.get)\n\n    # Fill gaps by nearest known diagonal class in the cyclic sequence.\n    known = list(seq)\n    for k in range(p):\n        if k not in seq:\n            near = min(known, key=lambda x: min((k-x) % p, (x-k) % p))\n            seq[k] = seq[near]\n\n    return [[seq[(c-r) % p] for c in range(w)] for r in range(h)]\n```\n{\"action\":\"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":137,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1790710595.048,"t1":1790710607.298,"alias":"task-1fde25f5","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 3 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n7 4 7 4 7 4 7\n4 7 4 7 4 7 4\n7 4 7 4 7 4 7\n4 7 4 7 4 7 4\n7 4 7 4 7 4 7\n4 7 4 7 4 7 4\n7 4 7 4 7 4 7\nwhere the pair's output is\n3 4 4 2 7 3 4\n4 4 2 7 3 4 4\n4 2 7 3 4 4 2\n2 7 3 4 4 2 7\n7 3 4 4 2 7 3\n3 4 4 2 7 3 4\n4 4 2 7 3 4 4\nFailed checks in this instance: 3 of 3. Reply with a corrected program and {\"action\": \"submit\"}, or with {\"action\": \"re